cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BioPhasor in your research, please cite the software and the manuscript below."
title: "BioPhasor: a phase-geometric platform for multi-omics"
abstract: >-
  A Python library and reproducible experiment suites that fit phasor geometry
  to omics measurements. Each feature is encoded as a complex phasor on the
  unit circle, so a sample is a point on the N-torus and circular statistics,
  spectral graph theory and coupled-oscillator dynamics apply directly. The
  package provides phasor encoding and circular operators, manifold geometry,
  the Cell State Tensor and its phase-coherence density matrix, Kuramoto and
  circadian dynamics, multi-omics fusion, and the spectral connectome in both
  its classical Hermitian form and a second-quantized Bose-Hubbard extension.
  The quantum vocabulary denotes a quantum-simulable formalism with an exact
  classical correspondence; no quantum advantage is claimed and no assertion is
  made that cells are quantum systems.
